From: Tiberiu Chibici <chibicitiberiu@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 12:31:56 +0200
Subject: nv30: on the PS3, index buffers are in GART by default; one found in
 VRAM moves there at its first indexed draw

The RSX driver fetches a draw's indices only from its own copies of index ranges in GART and
refuses an index buffer in VRAM (ps3rsx, the index copies). NV30_PS3_IDX_GART (0059) is
therefore on by default on the PS3: a buffer made as an index buffer (and not also as a vertex
buffer) is created in GART and only the CPU writes it. NV30_PS3_IDX_GART=0 keeps the old
placement, for a measurement against an older ps3rsx; the current one refuses it. Off the PS3
nothing changes.

A buffer used for indices that went to VRAM because it was made for another use first (a
vertex buffer, a buffer with no bind) moves to GART at its first indexed draw on the GPU path,
for good (nv30_idxbuf_to_gart): one GPU copy of its contents, CPU-written from then on like the
others, and the arrays validated again since it may be one of them. The copy is kicked in a
submission of its own: the kernel's copy of the indices waits for a GPU write into them that
is still in flight, but refuses a draw whose indices a GPU write earlier in the same submission
touched. Without room in GART the buffer stays in VRAM and the kernel refuses the draw.

Forwarded: no

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv30/nv30_resource.c b/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv30/nv30_resource.c
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv30/nv30_resource.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv30/nv30_resource.c
@@ -68,6 +68,29 @@ nv30_resource_create(struct pipe_screen *pscreen,
    }
 }
 
+/*
+ * NV30_PS3_IDX_GART: ps3rsx copies a draw's indices only out of GART and refuses an index buffer in
+ * VRAM, so a buffer that went to VRAM because it was made for another use (a vertex buffer, a buffer
+ * with no bind) moves to GART at its first indexed draw, for good, written by the CPU from then on
+ * (cpu_only, as nv30_resource_create's index buffers). The GPU's copy of its contents is kicked in a
+ * submission of its own: the kernel's copy of the indices waits for a GPU write still in flight, where
+ * one earlier in the same submission would get the draw refused. The arrays are validated again (the
+ * buffer may be one of them). false: no room in GART, the buffer stays in VRAM.
+ */
+bool
+nv30_idxbuf_to_gart(struct nv30_context *nv30, struct nv04_resource *res)
+{
+   if (res->domain != NOUVEAU_BO_VRAM)
+      return true;
+   if (!nouveau_buffer_migrate(&nv30->base, res, NOUVEAU_BO_GART))
+      return false;
+   res->cpu_only = 1;
+   nv30->dirty |= NV30_NEW_ARRAYS;
+   nv30->base.vbo_dirty = true;
+   PUSH_KICK(nv30->base.pushbuf);
+   return true;
+}
+
 static void
 nv30_resource_destroy(struct pipe_screen *pscreen, struct pipe_resource *res)
 {
diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv30/nv30_resource.h b/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv30/nv30_resource.h
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv30/nv30_resource.h
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv30/nv30_resource.h
@@ -68,6 +68,11 @@ nv30_miptree_get_handle(struct pipe_screen *pscreen,
 void
 nv30_miptree_destroy(struct pipe_screen *pscreen, struct pipe_resource *pt);
 
+struct nv30_context;
+struct nv04_resource;
+bool
+nv30_idxbuf_to_gart(struct nv30_context *nv30, struct nv04_resource *res);
+
 void
 nv30_resource_copy_region(struct pipe_context *pipe,
                           struct pipe_resource *dst, unsigned dst_level,
